g tissues, anemia\n  Favours second: abnormal bleeding, abnormal granulocytopoietic cell morphology, acute promyelocytic leukemia, alcoholism, anorexia\n\nDe Novo Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia (ALL) vs Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML) with Cytogenetic Abnormalities:\n  Favours first:  autosomal dominant somatic cell mutation, balance problems, bleeding from the gums, blurred vision, cellular immunodeficiency\n  Favours second: abdominal pain, abnormal bleeding, abnormal granulocytopoietic cell morphology, acute promyelocytic leukemia, alcoholism\n\nDe Novo Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia (ALL) vs Acute Promyelocytic Leukemia (APL), Subtype of AML:\n  Favours first:  autosomal dominant somatic cell mutation, balance problems, bleeding from the gums, blurred vision, cellular immunodeficiency\n  Favours second: abdominal pain, abnormal bleeding, abnormal granulocytopoietic cell morphology, acute promyelocytic leukemia, alcoholism\n\nRelated to Chronic Myeloid Leukemia in Blast Crisis (CML-BC): chronic myelogenous leukemia, bcr-abl1 positive\n\nRelated to De Novo Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia (ALL): acute lymphoblastic leukemia (disease), acute lymphoblastic/lymphocytic leukemia, childhood leukemia\n\nRelated to Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML) with Cytogenetic Abnormalities: acute myeloid leukemia with recurrent genetic anomaly\n\nRelated to Acute Promyelocytic Leukemia (APL), Subtype of AML: acute myeloid leukemia with recurrent genetic anomaly, bilineal acute myeloid leukemia\n\n[Indirect reasoning chains (PrimeKG 2-hop):]\n  and night sweats → fatigue → Chronic Myeloid Leukemia in Blast Crisis (CML-BC)\n  and night sweats → gangrene → Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML) with Cytogenetic Abnormalities\n  and night sweats → fatigue → Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML) with Cytogenetic Abnormalities"}
